`nautobot-ai-models` (>=1.1.0,<2.0.0, with its `discovery` extra) is now a required dependency, and `nautobot_ai_models` must be added to `PLUGINS` alongside this app. It is deliberately not optional and not behind an extra: `models.py` declares foreign keys into its tables, so Django resolves them at import time on every start, and a Nautobot that enables this app without that one will not start. litellm and the MCP client stay optional for the reason they always were - they are only ever called, and a deployment that calls neither installs neither. The floor is 1.1 rather than 1.0 because 1.1 is the release that records a provider's dialect and whether it is enabled, a model's kind and its generation parameters, and the two MCP registry-policy settings [ADR 0007](../docs/decisions/0007-mcp-tools-streamable-http-and-default-deny.md) relies on.
